# Halcyon's leaders: the research director at the lab and the field leads.
# Voice: precise, a bit cold, sometimes guilty. Humour only by accident: exact words that land wrong.
# Lines are spoken straight to the player (docs/WRITING.md, "Conversations"): who they are, where
# you are and what's going on, in their own words.

# The first time you meet one (a greet: the talk screen opens on it). One line, said only to a
# stranger (!met); the season's name (names.rzd) and a caught lie come first when they apply.
conv halcyon.leader.hello
for stronghold:halcyon, seat:halcyon/field_lead
when !met
greet
once
prio flavour
voice halcyon

node start
  say? bite_shown & !met :: I'm {npc}, {role}. That bite is recent, by the colour. The trial dose is free, once, at our stores: eight in ten walk out. Please go now. We can talk after.
  say? stronghold & !met :: I'm {npc}, {role}. This is the only lab in the Zone, and the cure is at {cure_percent} percent. The cure is what opens the gates. Please don't touch the cold boxes.
  say? !met :: I'm {npc}, {role}. This is a Halcyon field station: sensors, a cold box and a radio to the lab. The cure is at {cure_percent} percent. Mind the sample cases.

conv halcyon.leader.beaks
for stronghold:halcyon, seat:halcyon/field_lead
topic "Why do people call you the beaks?"
prio flavour
voice halcyon

node start
  say The respirators. Long filters, and the hoods. From a distance we look like birds, apparently, or old plague doctors. The Zone noticed before we did.
  say Somebody stencilled a plague doctor on a sample case as a joke. By the time anyone senior noticed, it was on every case, door and van we own.
  > @scrub Why not scrub it off? -> scrub
  > @notebook You still keep a notebook each? -> notebook   if bg:labtech,doctor,nurse
  > @other Let me ask about something else. -> hub

node scrub
  say Nobody could think of a reason that was worth the solvent. We're short of solvent.
  say Also, people step out of our way on the road. That has measurable value.
  > @back1 I suppose it does. Something else. -> hub

node notebook
  say Numbered, one each. Every reading, every sample, every volunteer. When one of us dies, the notebook belongs to the lab.
  say We read it into the record, page by page. It takes longer than the funeral. The director speaks for two minutes and goes back to work.
  do learn:halcyon.notebooks
  > @back2 That's a hard way to grieve. -> hub

conv halcyon.leader.numbers
for stronghold:halcyon, seat:halcyon/field_lead
when !epilogue
topic "How close is the cure?"
prio world
voice halcyon

node start
  say The number this morning was {cure_percent} percent. I wouldn't repeat it to anyone with a gun. People make plans around numbers.
  say The trial dose is the part that works today. Anyone bitten can have it once, for nothing. Eight in ten walk out. We write down the other two.
  > @two Who sits with the other two? -> two
  > @help What would speed it up? -> help
  > @hundred What happens when it reaches a hundred? -> hundred
  > @other3 Let me ask about something else. -> hub

node two
  say Someone with a clipboard. Somebody has to, and they should be counted: by name if the family gives one, by number if not.
  say It isn't a good job. It's a necessary one. Those aren't the same thing, and I've stopped pretending they are.
  > @back3 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node help
  say Samples. Live tissue from the big ones, cold and labelled, under six hours old. And time, which nobody can bring us.
  say? need:samples :: We're short this week. The field stations will pay for anything usable.
  say Ask the quartermaster what pays. I don't handle money. I handle consequences.
  > @back4 I'll ask. Something else. -> hub

node hundred
  say A cure isn't only a dose. It's proof: proof the Zone can be made clean, which is the one thing the people outside said would lift the quarantine.
  say Our Institute's last call, on Day 2, said exactly that. Then the line went dead. We've been working toward one sentence ever since.
  > @back5 Then I hope you finish it. -> hub

# A field lead who hides the other two: the lie, and the truth that opens a better answer
# (the Doctor wanderer says it too: dialogue/wanderers/lies.rzd).
conv halcyon.lead.volunteers
for seat:halcyon/field_lead
when cure>=25
topic "What happens to the volunteers?"
prio world
voice halcyon

node start
  say Anyone bitten can volunteer for the trial dose, once. The first ten came up from the Haven on Day 6, and eight walked out.
  say It's been eight in ten ever since, which is a coincidence. We write down the other two. They're in the record.
  > @where Where are the other two now? -> deflect
  > @sheets Ten went in. Your beds say eight. -> back_room   if bg:labtech,doctor
  > @catch There's a room at the back. I know. -> back_room   callout halcyon.back_room
  > @leave That's enough for me. -> hub

node deflect
  say Somewhere quiet, where they can rest. They're comfortable. Ask me something else. ~lie:halcyon.back_room
  > @show Then show me where they are. -> back_room | refused   check persuade halcyon 3 bg:labtech,doctor
  > @drop All right. Something else. -> hub

node refused
  say No. And if you're from the houses, tell them we're sorry. We are.
  > @yourself Tell them yourself. -> start
  > @drop2 Let me ask something else. -> hub

node back_room
  say There's a room at the back of the station. Someone sits with them, with a clipboard and a sample kit, until they turn. It's the protocol, and I hate it. ~truth:halcyon.back_room
  > @back1 Thank you for telling me. -> hub
